# ---- Serving artifacts: tracked so a deployment can actually start ----
# A container built from this repo has no models otherwise, and PolicyRouter
# loads policy_track_a.pt in its constructor — so the API crashes on the first
# request rather than at build time. This is the minimum set that answers
# requests, ~11 MB in total. Negations must come after the patterns above, and
# a negation cannot re-include a file whose PARENT directory is excluded, which
# is why each `backend/models/...` line is spelled out rather than globbed.
!backend/models/policy_track_a.pt
!backend/models/policy_track_b.pt
!backend/models/normaliser_stats.json
!backend/models/normaliser_stats_track_b.json
!backend/models/ood_ae_track_a.pt
!backend/models/feature_imputer_track_b.pkl
!backend/models/action_map.json

# 56 KB each: the pre-subsampled states the decision-rule tree is fitted from at
# startup. The full MDP parquets stay out — 42 MB for track A, and reading it
# costs enough RSS to OOM a small instance (see backend/api/state.py::_distil).
!backend/data/processed/mdp_track_a_treesample.parquet
!backend/data/processed/mdp_track_b_treesample.parquet

# The OPE results /api/validation reads. Small JSON, no patient rows.
!backend/logs/behaviour_track_a.json
!backend/logs/fqe_track_a.json
!backend/logs/dfqe_track_a.json
!backend/logs/nwe_track_a.json
!backend/logs/cv_track_a.json
!backend/logs/ablation_track_b.json
*.db
ventassist.db
